Unreleased
---
Feature
- The library opens. It is the shared base the control libraries draw on:
  the mechanisms two design languages answer the same way - state layers,
  focus rings, shadows - kept apart from the forms, which stay with each
  family. It reads the token vocabularies from qxtheme and nothing above it.
- QxStateLayer, the wash a control draws over itself to say where the pointer
  is, where the focus sits, what is being pressed: default opacities per
  state, layered() as the value a test can predict, paint() as the draw.
  Which colour a family washes with belongs to the family; how a wash is
  composed and painted is here.
